Performance: SDD

Purpose:
  Performance testing — verify system performance meets non-functional
  requirements. Performance tests measure response time, throughput,
  resource usage, and scalability.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  Response time
  Throughput (requests per second)
  Resource usage (CPU, memory, disk, network)
  Database query performance
  Cache hit rates
  Concurrency behavior

Principles:
  Test against defined NFRs, not arbitrary thresholds
  Measure baselines before optimizing
  Test in production-like environment
  Profile before optimizing
  Performance regressions block release

Structure:
  Every performance test MUST:
    define clear NFR targets
    measure against those targets
    produce actionable results
    compare against baseline

Frameworks:
  k6
  Gatling
  JMeter
  Lighthouse (frontend)
  Xdebug/pprof (profiling)

Navigation:
  Project: @project/project.sdd
  Workflow: @workflow/testing.sdd
  TestLevels: @levels.sdd
  TestTypes: @types.sdd
  TestGates: @gates.sdd
  Load: @load.sdd
  ProjectTesting: @projects/{project_name}/testing/INDEX.sdd

State: +
  